---
layout: base.njk
title: "Pockit Course"
description: "Write your course once — print it as pocket-sized lesson cards, or share it as a responsive web page. No sign-up required."
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>The workbook is dead. Long live the workbook!</h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        <strong>The Pockit Course is an ingenious DIY publishing tool</strong> for making tactile workbooks in our last-minute, chronically-distracted classrooms.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="hero-cta" href="/course-builder/">Make a Pockit Course now!</a>
        <span class="hero-cta-note">No sign in required.</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Decorative hand-drawn-style arrow pointing down from the CTA
           to the "Why the Pockit Course?" heading below — calibrated
           (see .hero-arrow in custom.css) against this page's actual
           layout at a ~1400px desktop viewport; hidden on narrow
           screens where the two-column hero collapses and the offsets
           no longer line up. Sits in normal flow right after the CTA
           row (so its start always tracks the button regardless of
           hero's own height, which is usually dominated by the taller
           card stack beside it) but the SVG itself breaks out below via
           absolute positioning to reach down into the next section. -->
      <div class="hero-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="280" height="420" viewBox="0 0 280 420">
          <path class="hero-arrow-curl" d="
            M 128 8
            C 120 40, 140 65, 115 95
            C 95 120, 60 130, 50 165
            C 40 195, 75 215, 100 245
            C 120 270, 75 290, 55 260
            C 38 235, 55 195, 90 200
            C 130 205, 175 225, 180 265
            C 185 300, 130 305, 125 340
            C 120 365, 160 383, 222 383
          "/>
          <polygon class="hero-arrow-head" points="222,377 222,389 233,383"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-image">
      <!-- A recreation of a real course-builder lesson card (see
           .card/.card-header/.card-footer in
           src/course-builder/css/style.css and buildCard() in
           src/course-builder/js/render-card.js) — same 80mm × 160mm size,
           header/footer structure, hole-punch and colours. Body content
           still TODO; for now it's just header + footer over a blank
           card. In front of it, offset to the left, the course's front
           cover (see #cover-front/#cover-front-mark/#cover-front-info in
           src/course-builder/index.html + css/style.css and
           renderCoverView() in js/course-builder.js) — same 81mm × 161mm
           size (1mm bigger than the card, same as the real cover), brand
           mark, code/title panel and handwritten name/contact prompt —
           so the card looks like it's sliding out from underneath it. -->
      <div class="hero-card-stack">
        <!-- A second card behind the front one, barely peeking out — just
             enough to read as a small stack of lesson cards, not a
             single one. -->
        <div class="hero-card-back"></div>

        <div class="hero-card">
          <div class="hero-card-header">
            <div class="hero-card-punch"></div>
            <div class="hero-card-header-stack">
              <div class="hero-card-header-text">Getting Started</div>
              <div class="hero-card-lesson-count">1 of 2</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Wireframe placeholders standing in for real card content —
               loosely modelled on course-builder's own block types (see
               BLOCK_TYPES in src/course-builder/js/block-types.js): a
               Heading, a Text block, a full-width Image block, another
               Text block, a Link (QR) block (mirrored from the real
               card's QR-on-the-left layout, purely for this stylised
               wireframe), then a Task/Reflection-style block (boxed,
               question line + blank ruled space for a written answer)
               pushed down to fill the rest of the card. -->
          <div class="hero-card-body">
            <span class="hero-card-wire-heading"></span>

            <div class="hero-card-wire-text">
              <span class="hero-card-wire-line"></span>
              <span class="hero-card-wire-line"></span>
              <span class="hero-card-wire-line is-short"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-card-wire-image">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/>
                <circle cx="8.5" cy="10" r="1.5"/>
                <path d="M21 16l-5-5-6 6-2-2-5 4"/>
              </svg>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-card-wire-text">
              <span class="hero-card-wire-line"></span>
              <span class="hero-card-wire-line is-short"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-card-wire-link">
              <div class="hero-card-wire-text hero-card-wire-link-text">
                <span class="hero-card-wire-line is-short"></span>
                <span class="hero-card-wire-line"></span>
              </div>
              <svg class="hero-card-wire-qr" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <!-- Finder squares (the three corner markers every real QR
                     code has). -->
                <rect x="1" y="1" width="6" height="6"/>
                <rect x="3" y="3" width="2" height="2"/>
                <rect x="17" y="1" width="6" height="6"/>
                <rect x="19" y="3" width="2" height="2"/>
                <rect x="1" y="17" width="6" height="6"/>
                <rect x="3" y="19" width="2" height="2"/>
                <!-- Scattered data cells, deliberately irregular rather than
                     evenly spaced, so it reads as noise rather than a
                     pattern — kept off the outer edge (a real QR code
                     always has a blank quiet zone around it) and out of
                     the finder squares' own corners above. -->
                <rect x="8" y="2" width="2" height="2"/>
                <rect x="10" y="2" width="2" height="2"/>
                <rect x="8" y="6" width="2" height="2"/>
                <rect x="12" y="6" width="2" height="2"/>
