  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-section">
  <div class="page-section-inner page-section-inner--wide page-section-inner--intro-left">
    <h2>Why the Pockit Course?</h2>
    <p class="page-section-intro">
      <strong>Tactile workbook-based learning is still the best.</strong> But we gave up on workbooks because they were too hard to maintain compared to throwing stuff online. Well, not anymore!
    </p>

    <!-- Two in-class photos, side by side, equal size (see
         .why-photo-row). -->
    <div class="why-photo-row">
      <img src="/images/in-class-03.jpg" alt="Two people writing notes on sticky notes laid out on a large sheet of paper.">
      <img src="/images/in-class-04.jpg" alt="A hand holding a folded printed booklet on a table, with a QR-coded card nearby.">
    </div>
    <p class="why-photo-caption">An earlier iteration of the Pockit Book that started it all &mdash; proved the value of the concept, and proved they were too much effort for a typical teacher to produce.</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <!-- 1. An end to death-by-PowerPoint — a widescreen slide behind,
           the Pockit card-shaped mark (same 80:160 rectangle used
           throughout — nav motif, cover mark) overtaking its corner. -->
      <!-- 1. Bring an end to death-by-PowerPoint — a whole deck (slides
           stacked/peeking behind the front one), a full-width title, a
           wall of bullets, two overlapping photos, and the universal
           "banned" circle-and-slash — thick and translucent — over the
           top of it. Full-bleed art at the top of the card, not a small
           icon — see .feature-item-art in custom.css. -->
      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-item-art">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 240">
            <rect width="400" height="240" fill="#f6f6f6"/>

            <!-- The slide, presented on a laptop screen — same laptop
                 treatment as icon 3. Scaled down around the icon's
                 centre for more padding around it. -->
            <g transform="translate(200 120) scale(0.82) translate(-200 -120)">
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="360" height="196" rx="10" fill="#ececec" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="2"/>
              <rect x="10" y="219" width="380" height="10" rx="5" fill="#ececec" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="2"/>
              <rect x="180" y="222" width="40" height="4" rx="2" fill="#ddd"/>
              <rect x="30" y="30" width="340" height="180" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="1.5"/>

              <!-- Title, right across the slide. -->
              <rect x="48" y="46" width="296" height="14" rx="3" fill="#ccc"/>

              <!-- Bullets. -->
              <circle cx="54" cy="82" r="3" fill="#bbb"/>
              <line x1="65" y1="82" x2="185" y2="82" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <circle cx="54" cy="98" r="3" fill="#bbb"/>
              <line x1="65" y1="98" x2="165" y2="98" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <circle cx="54" cy="114" r="3" fill="#bbb"/>
              <line x1="65" y1="114" x2="190" y2="114" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
