              <line x1="166" y1="86" x2="234" y2="154" stroke="#e8a8a3" stroke-width="12" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Bring an end to death-by-PowerPoint</h3>
        <p>They're not fun to create and they're not fun to receive. Break out of the mindset, while still thinking in learning blocks.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. Publish as you go — a bound book (banned, same style as
           the slide deck above) on one side; an arrow across to a
           folder with individual cards spilling out of it on the
           other — one big workbook replaced by a growing set of
           cards, not by nothing. -->
      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-item-art">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 240">
            <rect width="400" height="240" fill="#f6f6f6"/>

            <!-- The old workbook — drawn obliquely (a slight tilt plus
                 a page-edge sliver down its right side) so it reads
